  "equipment_type": "Thermal dispersion airflow measuring station",
  "applies_to": "EBTRON Gold Series GTx116 transmitters: GTC116 (RS-485) and GTM116 (Ethernet) network models.",
  "summary": "The Gold Series GTx116 is EBTRON's earlier (Advantage III) airflow transmitter. Over BACnet it reports average airflow, average temperature and alarm status, plus optional per-probe flow and temperature traverse values. GTC116 boards speak BACnet MS/TP (default 76,800 baud) or Modbus RTU; GTM116 boards speak BACnet IP or BACnet Ethernet, with Modbus TCP always on.",
  "bacnet_transport": [
    "BACnet MS/TP",
    "BACnet IP",
    "BACnet Ethernet"
  ],
  "firmware": null,
  "default_device_instance": 2,
  "access_inferred": true,
  "notes": [
    "Factory device instance is 2 on both GTC116 and GTM116; change it from the NETWORK menu or by writing the Device object identifier.",
    "GTM116 default IP is 10.0.0.100/255.255.255.0, gateway 10.0.0.10, DHCP off; use UDP port 47808.",
    "Traverse objects AV3-AV34 only carry data after AV2 is set to Flow, Temp or Both.",
    "The 16 flow traverse and 16 temperature traverse objects share the names printed in the manual; check actual object names on site.",
    "Supported services listed: Subscribe COV, ReadProperty, WriteProperty, DeviceCommunicationControl, Who-Is."
  ],
